Z||000024||TwisT||03-04-2001||07:33 PM||||The bumber of the whole online-forum type of communication is that it makes it WAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAYYYYYYYYY TO EASY for people to type in words behind a computer screen on how they DON'T like your style or method of expression.  <P>It never fails...  every post I've EVER made in this forum results in someone poking at my ideas,  like,  "I don't like this...  I don't like that...  that looks like something a ricer would do...  I wouldn't do that...  blah blah blah."<P>My attitude is to just 'consider the source' but it still remains frustrating.  People are rude,  plain and simple.  It's the open-minded and contributing members of this (or any forum) that keep me and everyone else coming back.<P>My advice...  get used to it...  Put up or shut up.  But don't join in on the bashing if you yourself don't like it done to you.<P>Brett      <P>||||reg||1
