Z||000029||billyboy||03-05-2001||12:00 AM||||Riceboy?  Lets look at the terminology.  Rice is *supposedly* what's used to drive Asian cars, right?  That's why they're called "rice burners", correct?  OK, I'm a male, and was once a boy, but without age specification, you could still call me a boy (even though I'm 24).  Here's my current line up that I drive:<P>86 Toyota MR2<BR>95 Subaru SVX<BR>91 Honda CBR600F2<P>Previous cars:<BR>92 Nissan Sentra SE-R<BR>89 Nissan Stanza GXE<BR>95 Nissan Altima SE<BR>88 Subaru XT6<BR>88 Subaru RX Turbo<BR>96 Toyota Tercel<P>Granted, some of the cars aren't gems or anything, but I've had my share of rice.  While I don't actually *own* a Fiero, I still like them, and I wouldn't mind owning an 88 Formula eventually.  I like all of you guys on this board, you're (normally) very friendly, inquisitive, and just fun to talk to.  I have a lot of respect for just about everyone on this board.<P>Anyway, if the term "riceboy" fits everything that I've listed here, then I'm proud to be a riceboy.<P>PS.  At the VERY least, I've never had a phantom top or huge wing on *any* of my cars... and I'm even a riceboy...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
